# Responsive & UI polish

## Responsive
- **Mobile-first**. Layouts must work on small screens and desktop.
- Dropdowns/modals/sheets must be **scrollable** when content overflows (never clipped off-screen).
- Touch targets usable on mobile; avoid overcrowding the header — use top bar vs main header thoughtfully.
- Test mental model: phone + tablet + desktop, not desktop-only.

## Clarity
- Prefer clear labels over cryptic shorthand (e.g. say "12 digits", not "12d").
- Counts in filters: show quantity up front when useful, e.g. `(1,204) +44 · United Kingdom`.
- Empty/loading/error states should be intentional and readable.

## Design system
- Use existing DS components (`@/components/ds/*`) and storefront CSS variables/patterns.
- Preserve established visual language; don't invent a second design system.
- Avoid generic AI-template aesthetics when building marketing/landing surfaces.
